[center][color=#f59e0b][size=6][b]R O M A N T A S Y[/b][/size][/color]
[color=#b8a285][size=3]A Ledger of Hearts.[/size][/color]
[color=#b8a285]A relationship framework for Skyrim SE/AE | Version 4.0.0[/color]

[color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]What's New in 4.0[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]The Rosewater ledger[/color] - the ledger and tier popups are now a page hosted by Magelight UI. [b]Magelight UI 1.6 or newer is now required.[/b]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Roster tools[/color] - find a companion by name, order the roster by Closest, Name or Recent, and see bonds grouped under Following and Away
[*][color=#fbbf24]A journal for every bond[/color] - the last 30 changes, a chart of the last sixty days, the biggest gains and losses, and milestones
[*][color=#fbbf24]Mood[/color] - every bond is Strained, Settled or Warm, and it drifts back to Settled over time
[*][color=#fbbf24]Favorites and pet peeves[/color] - up to three of each per personality; a favorite counts double, a pet peeve costs double
[*][color=#fbbf24]Tier unlock lines[/color] - follower authors can name what each tier brings, and the tier popup lists it
[*][color=#fbbf24]Whispers[/color] - short cards on the HUD that say what just moved a bond, without pausing anything
[*][color=#fbbf24]Calm-moment popups[/color] - tier popups wait until you are out of combat and somewhere peaceful, never longer than a day
[*][color=#fbbf24]Relationship pace[/color] - Slow burn, Standard or Fast
[*][color=#fbbf24]Comfort settings[/color] - Ledger size, Stronger contrast and Reduce motion
[*][color=#fbbf24]Safer saves[/color] - a bond survives its follower's mod going missing, and player-made bonds are now saved with the game
[*][color=#fbbf24]Health[/color] - a section in Settings that tells you whether Romantasy is working and what is wrong if it is not
[*][color=#fbbf24]Optional bridges[/color] - SkyrimNet and OStim Standalone, both switched off automatically when the mod is not installed
[*][color=#fbbf24]Translatable[/color] - almost every word the ledger shows lives in one file
[*][color=#fbbf24]For follower authors[/color] - an author test kit, a "why" log for every deed, new events and a smarter profile checker
[/list]

[color=#f43f5e][b]Important:[/b] do not load a save made with 4.0.0 in Romantasy 3.0.1 or older. Those versions skip the new save records, and the bond points in that save would be lost.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Author's Note[/color][/b][/size]

I wanted romance in Skyrim to grow out of the way you actually play, not out of a menu. Romantasy watches the adventure you are already having and quietly turns it into a bond, one dungeon, one quest, one bad decision at a time. It does not replace your follower mods and it does not write anyone's personality. It only keeps the ledger.

Followers can arrive with a personality written by their author, or you can create one yourself for any follower who does not have one, right from the dashboard. Either way, the adventure is what moves the relationship.

If you are a mod author and you build something on top of it, please tell me. I would genuinely love to play it.


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Overview[/color][/b][/size]

[b][color=#fbbf24]A standalone, save-safe relationship system that turns the way you play into a deepening bond with each of your followers.[/color][/b]
Six tiers, one ledger, zero micromanagement.

Romantasy tracks your deeds across [color=#fbbf24]58 categories of play[/color] (combat, exploration, crafting, crime, guild work, vampire and werewolf life, and more) and turns them into relationship points for every follower it manages. Each follower has her own likes and dislikes, and now her own favorites and pet peeves. Do what she loves and the bond deepens. Do what she hates and it wounds.

The bond climbs through six tiers: [color=#fbbf24]Stranger[/color], [color=#fbbf24]Acquaintance[/color], [color=#fbbf24]Friend[/color], [color=#fbbf24]Confidant[/color], [color=#fbbf24]Lover[/color] and [color=#fbbf24]Spouse[/color]. Follower mods can hang dialogue, scenes, voiced reactions, quest beats or marriage hooks off any of them.

Romantasy slots underneath your existing follower mods without taking them over. It does not replace the vanilla follower system, Horde, NFF, AFT, EFF, custom follower controllers or the vanilla marriage system. It is the scoreboard; the follower's author is still the writer.

[color=#b8a285][b]Note:[/b] the plugin is ESL-flagged, the SKSE DLL is digitally signed, and bonds, points, moods and journals are stored in each save's SKSE co-save.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Features[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]The Ledger[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Rosewater ledger[/color] - a full-screen page hosted by Magelight UI, with your company beside the selected bond's dossier
[*][color=#fbbf24]Your Company[/color] - every bond with its points, tier, progress and Following or Away status
[*][color=#fbbf24]Find, order, group[/color] - type in Find a companion to filter by name, choose an Order (Closest, Name or Recent), and read bonds grouped under Following and Away
[*][color=#fbbf24]Dossier[/color] - mood, What they value, Recent changes (the last five), Personality and Milestones, including how far the bond is from the next tier and what that tier unlocks
[*][color=#fbbf24]Journal[/color] - the full story of a bond: History, The last sixty days chart, Deepened most and Wounded most, and Milestones such as each tier reached or lost
[*][color=#fbbf24]New bond[/color] - give any follower without author support a personality: stamp each deed Like, Dislike, Favorite, Pet peeve or Neutral, with a search box across seven categories of deeds
[*][color=#fbbf24]Bond tools[/color] - Edit personality, Reset bond and Remove bond for bonds you made yourself; reset and remove ask first
[*][color=#fbbf24]Protected author profiles[/color] - personalities supplied by follower authors are sealed and marked Author-defined personality; nothing can overwrite them
[*][color=#fbbf24]Comfort settings[/color] - Ledger size (Standard, Large, Largest), Stronger contrast and Reduce motion; the tier popup follows them too
[*][color=#fbbf24]Keyboard, mouse and gamepad[/color] - all three move through the ledger, with button hints for whichever you are holding; typing needs a keyboard
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Bonds That Feel Alive[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Six tiers[/color] - from Stranger to Spouse, 500 points apart; bonds can fall as well as rise
[*][color=#fbbf24]Mood[/color] - gains warm a bond, losses strain it, and each in-game day it drifts back toward Settled; mood never changes points or tiers
[*][color=#fbbf24]Favorites and pet peeves[/color] - the deeds she cares about most count double, in either direction
[*][color=#fbbf24]Tier unlock lines[/color] - an author can write a few lines per tier ("A key to her house"); the dossier shows what the next tier brings and the popup lists it under Unlocked
[*][color=#fbbf24]Whispers[/color] - a small card in a corner of the HUD, such as "Dungeons Cleared · +2" or "Glad to have you back", for about four seconds; one at a time, never pausing the game, and they wait out menus and dialogue
[*][color=#fbbf24]Tier popups[/color] - Romance Deepened in gold, Romance Wounded in rose, each with its own music; they do not pause the game and close themselves after 20 seconds
[*][color=#fbbf24]A calm moment[/color] - by default a tier popup waits until you are out of combat and in an inn, a home, a town, or waking from sleep; it never waits longer than one in-game day, and several changes for one bond arrive as one
[*][color=#fbbf24]Relationship pace[/color] - Fast doubles the points from deeds; Slow burn halves them and asks for days together before each higher tier (Friend 3, Confidant 7, Lover 14, Spouse 21); losses are never changed
[*][color=#fbbf24]Reunions and time apart[/color] - Romantasy notices when a companion has been away for days and when she comes back
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Safe Saves[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Bonds survive a missing mod[/color] - if a follower's plugin is not loaded, her points and journal are kept and written back on every save, and return with her mod; a HUD line says how many bonds are being kept
[*][color=#fbbf24]Player-made bonds live in the save[/color] - New bond saves the personality with the game, so Remove bond only affects the current save
[*][color=#fbbf24]Load order changes are fine[/color] - bonds are keyed by plugin name and local ID, not by load order position
[*][color=#fbbf24]Health[/color] - a section in Settings that names anything wrong (Magelight UI missing or too old, an outdated plugin, rejected personality files, a damaged save record, settings that could not be saved) and marks the Settings button when something needs a look
[*][color=#fbbf24]Crash-safe files[/color] - settings and personality files are replaced whole, so a crash while saving cannot leave half a file
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Optional Integrations[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]SkyrimNet[/color] - with SkyrimNet's AI-driven dialogue installed, a bonded companion knows her tier, mood and days together, hears about tier changes and reunions, and a kind word (+5) or a harsh one (-5) in conversation can nudge the bond, at most one of each an hour and 15 a day each way
[*][color=#fbbf24]OStim Standalone[/color] - quiet time alone with a bonded companion in a scene counts as a shared moment: a small gain, once a day, that never costs the bond; popups and whispers also wait until a scene is over
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]Both bridges switch themselves off when their mod is not installed, and each has its own rows in Settings that appear only when the mod is found.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]The Six Tiers[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Stranger[/color] - 0 points
[*][color=#fbbf24]Acquaintance[/color] - 500 points
[*][color=#fbbf24]Friend[/color] - 1,000 points
[*][color=#fbbf24]Confidant[/color] - 1,500 points
[*][color=#fbbf24]Lover[/color] - 2,000 points
[*][color=#fbbf24]Spouse[/color] - 2,500 points
[/list]

A follower who watches you do the things she hates will drift back down through the tiers, and the ledger will show you the damage.

[color=#b8a285][b]Note:[/b] Spouse is a Romantasy relationship tier. It does not perform Skyrim's vanilla marriage, and adding a bond does not give a follower new voiced dialogue.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Requirements[/color][/b][/size]

[list]
[*]Skyrim Special Edition 1.5.97 or a supported Anniversary Edition runtime
[*][url=https://skse.silverlock.org/]SKSE64[/url] matching your Skyrim runtime
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/skyrimspecialedition/mods/32444]Address Library for SKSE Plugins[/url] matching your Skyrim runtime
[*]Magelight UI 1.6 or newer - hosts the ledger, the tier popups and the whispers
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Optional[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*]SkyrimNet, a recent version - for the bond line, events and conversation nudges; Health says if yours is too old
[*]OStim Standalone 7.3.3 or newer - for shared moments and quiet during scenes (7.4 or newer for a follower mod to start a moment)
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]Not needed: Meridian UI, Prisma UI, Media Keys Fix, SkyUI or an MCM. Skyrim VR is not supported by the ledger. Without Magelight UI the ledger cannot open, but points are still tracked.[/color]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Installation[/color][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Install SKSE64, Address Library and Magelight UI 1.6 or newer.
[*]Install Romantasy with your mod manager (MO2, Vortex, etc.). Keep the bundled page files, scripts, sounds and licenses.
[*]Activate [font=Courier New]CS_Romantasy.esp[/font] in your load order.
[*]If a follower offers Romantasy support as a separate download, install it alongside the follower.
[*]Launch the game, open the ledger with Left Ctrl + R and check that Health in Settings says everything is in order.
[*]Go adventuring.
[/list]

There is no MCM, no INI to edit and no quest to start. Romantasy can be added mid-playthrough; a new bond begins at 0 unless the follower's author sets a starting tier.

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]Upgrading[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]From 3.x[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install Magelight UI 1.6 or newer. The ledger and popups need it now.
[*]Install 4.0.0 over your previous version. Points, personalities and settings carry over.
[*]Load your save. Bonds you made yourself are written into the save from now on; the files in [font=Courier New]PlayerProfiles[/font] stay as copies, so keep that folder.
[*]Make a new save. Protection for bonds whose follower mod is missing starts with the first save made with 4.0.0.
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]From 2.x[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install Magelight UI 1.6 or newer. Meridian UI is no longer needed; keep it only if another mod asks for it.
[*]Install 4.0.0 over your previous version. Your saves keep their points.
[*]Bonds you created yourself in 2.x migrate the first time each follower is loaded, keeping likes, dislikes and points.
[*]If you opened Romantasy with LB + X, turn on Open with Favorites Menu in Settings and use the Romantasy power instead.
[/list]

[color=#f43f5e][b]Important:[/b] a save written by 4.0.0 must not be loaded in 3.0.1 or older. Those versions skip the new save records, so the bond points in that save would be lost. Keep an older save if you might go back.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]How to Use[/color][/b][/size]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Opening the Ledger[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Left Ctrl + R[/color] - opens or closes the ledger (the default)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Romantasy power[/color] - turn on Open with Favorites Menu in Settings and Romantasy gives you a lesser power, already favorited; cast it to open the ledger. The hotkey is off while this is on.
[/list]

The ledger pauses the game while it is open. Tier popups and whispers do not.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Controls[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Keyboard[/color] - arrow keys or Tab to move, Enter to select, Esc to go back or close
[*][color=#fbbf24]Gamepad[/color] - D-pad to move, A to select, B to go back or close
[*][color=#fbbf24]Mouse[/color] - click anything; hover a day in the journal chart to see its numbers
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]Esc or B steps back one layer at a time: popup, confirmation, New bond page, Settings or Journal, then the ledger itself. Typing, such as searching deeds or finding a companion, needs a keyboard.[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Making a New Bond[/color][/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Recruit a follower who has no author support and bring her along.
[*]Open the ledger and choose [color=#fbbf24]New bond[/color].
[*]Pick the companion, then stamp the deeds that deepen or wound the bond. Every deed starts Neutral; three favorites and three pet peeves at most.
[*]Choose [color=#fbbf24]Begin bond[/color]. The bond starts at 0 points.
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]Followers created at runtime by other mods, without a stable plugin record, cannot be added. A copy of each personality is written to [font=Courier New]SKSE/Plugins/Romantasy/PlayerProfiles[/font] (under MO2, usually in Overwrite).[/color]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]The Journal[/color][/b][/size]

Select a bond and choose [color=#fbbf24]Journal[/color] at the foot of the Recent changes card. It shows the History of the last 30 changes, The last sixty days as a chart of points gained and lost, the five moments that Deepened most and Wounded most, and Milestones: when the journal began, each tier reached, each fall, and A first moment together. Days are counted from Day 1 of the save. The journal only records; it never changes a bond.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Settings[/color][/b][/size]

Open [color=#fbbf24]Settings[/color] from the roster. Every row is listed below with its default.

[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Open with Favorites Menu[/color] - cast the Romantasy power instead of using Left Ctrl + R (default: off)
[*][color=#fbbf24]"Romance Deepened" popups[/color] - the gold popup when a bond rises a tier (default: on)
[*][color=#fbbf24]"Romance Wounded" popups[/color] - the rose popup when a bond slips a tier (default: on)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Show away companions[/color] - keep bonds in the roster when they are not following (default: on)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Tier changes arrive[/color] - At a calm moment or At once (default: At a calm moment)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Relationship pace[/color] - Slow burn, Standard or Fast (default: Standard)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Whispers[/color] - small notes on the HUD when a companion reacts (default: on)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Whisper corner[/color] - Top left, Top right, Bottom left or Bottom right (default: Top right)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Tell SkyrimNet about bonds[/color] - shown only with SkyrimNet (default: on)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Conversations can move the bond[/color] - shown only with SkyrimNet (default: on)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Shared moments[/color] - shown only with OStim (default: on)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Quiet during scenes[/color] - shown only with OStim (default: on)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Ledger size[/color] - Standard, Large or Largest (default: Standard)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Stronger contrast[/color] - brighter text, solid panels and thicker outlines (default: off)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Reduce motion[/color] - stops the drifting backdrop and the larger animations (default: off)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Detailed log[/color] - writes every point change, and why, to [font=Courier New]Romantasy.log[/font] (default: off)
[*][color=#fbbf24]Developer tools[/color] - password-protected testing buttons (default: locked)
[/list]

The [color=#fbbf24]Health[/color] section sits at the foot of the list when all is well, and jumps to the top when something needs attention.

[color=#b8a285]Settings are saved to [font=Courier New]Data/SKSE/Plugins/Romantasy/settings.json[/font] and apply to every save.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]How It Works[/color][/b][/size]

[color=#fbbf24][b]Watching the adventure[/b][/color] - Romantasy listens to the same statistics the game already keeps. Clear a dungeon, finish a quest, pick a pocket, read a skill book: when the game records it, Romantasy asks each follower who is with you whether she cares. A like adds the deed's points, a dislike takes them away, a favorite or pet peeve doubles either, and no opinion means nothing happens.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Only shared adventures count[/b][/color] - points from deeds go only to a managed follower who is actively following you. Someone waiting at home does not react. A follower who has just come into the loaded area may take a few seconds to start earning.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Mood[/b][/color] - gains warm a bond and losses strain it. Each in-game day the mood drifts back toward Settled. Mood colours the dossier, dialogue can read it, and it never moves points or tiers.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Pacing[/b][/color] - Relationship pace scales the points from deeds: double on Fast, half on Slow burn. Slow burn also asks for days together before each higher tier, and the dossier shows the gate ahead. A gate never takes points away. Losses and a follower author's own scripted amounts are never scaled.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Shared moments[/b][/color] - with OStim installed, time alone with one bonded companion in a scene can count as a shared moment. It needs just the two of you, at least 20 seconds, nothing marked as force, and a bond that has reached the tier where she welcomes that kind of moment (Friend, Confidant or Lover by default). A moment adds 5 points once a day (10 for a companion who treasures them), never costs the bond and never strains the mood. The journal names it only by its kind, such as A tender moment. Switch it off any time with Shared moments.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Personalities and points[/b][/color] - a personality comes from a profile file supplied by the follower's author, or from you through New bond. Author personalities are sealed. Earned points, moods, journals and player-made bonds all live in your save, so every save keeps its own story.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Saves[/b][/color] - bonds are keyed by the follower's plugin name and local ID. If that plugin is missing, the bond is kept and written back on every save until it returns. A damaged record in the co-save costs only the entries after the damage.

[color=#fbbf24][b]Performance[/b][/color] - the tracker is native SKSE code that reacts to the game's statistic events. There are no Papyrus polling loops, and the ledger only draws while it is open.


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]For Mod Authors[/color][/b][/size]

Romantasy is a modding resource. You keep full control of your follower's dialogue, scenes, personality, pacing and marriage content. Romantasy supplies the ledger, the tiers, the queries and the events. Your follower plugin does not need Romantasy as a master, and players without Romantasy keep your follower exactly as she is.

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]What You Can Do[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][color=#fbbf24]Personality file[/color] - one small TOML file in [font=Courier New]SKSE/Plugins/Romantasy/Profiles/[/font] with likes, dislikes, up to three favorites and three pet peeves, a starting tier, unlock lines per tier, and a moments table for the tiers she welcomes each kind of moment and how she feels about them
[*][color=#fbbf24]Dialogue conditions[/color] - [font=Courier New]GetGraphVariableInt[/font] run on Subject with [font=Courier New]Romantasy_Registered[/font], [font=Courier New]Romantasy_Level[/font], [font=Courier New]Romantasy_Points[/font] or [font=Courier New]Romantasy_Mood[/font]; no factions or scripts needed
[*][color=#fbbf24]Papyrus script[/color] - [font=Courier New]Romantasy.psc[/font] (capability version 9) to award or remove points at a scripted beat, read points, tier and mood, and ask for or start a shared moment
[*][color=#fbbf24]Events[/color] - [font=Courier New]Romantasy_OnLevelChanged[/font], [font=Courier New]Romantasy_OnLevelLost[/font], [font=Courier New]Romantasy_OnPreference[/font], [font=Courier New]Romantasy_OnTimeApart[/font], [font=Courier New]Romantasy_OnReunion[/font], [font=Courier New]Romantasy_OnSharedMoment[/font] and [font=Courier New]Romantasy_OnMomentRefused[/font] for voiced reactions
[*][color=#fbbf24]Author test kit[/color] - set [font=Courier New]"authorMode": true[/font] by hand in [font=Courier New]settings.json[/font] to unlock debug functions that fire a deed, set points, days together or mood, and announce a waiting tier now; with Detailed log on, every deed writes a [font=Courier New]why:[/font] line saying what changed and why, or why nothing did
[*][color=#fbbf24]Profile checker[/color] - [font=Courier New]tools/romantasy-profile-check.exe[/font] checks a file or folder of profiles without starting the game, with [font=Courier New]--strict[/font] and [font=Courier New]--json[/font]
[*][color=#fbbf24]SkyrimNet and OStim hooks[/color] - the SkyrimNet bond line and events come for free; the OStim moment functions and events let your follower ask for a gentle moment of her own
[*][color=#fbbf24]Older integrations[/color] - runtime registration, the [font=Courier New]ROM_*[/font] faction tags and faction-rank conditions from 2.x keep working
[/list]

[size=4][b][color=#d99563]Documents in the Mod's docs Folder[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][font=Courier New]AuthorGuide.md[/font] - start here: the shortest path from a follower to a supported follower
[*][font=Courier New]FileProfiles.md[/font] - personality files, unlock lines, moments, New bond and dialogue conditions
[*][font=Courier New]papyrus-bridge.md[/font] - every Papyrus function and event
[*][font=Courier New]romance-points-dialogue-conditions.md[/font] - dialogue conditions in detail
[*][font=Courier New]AuthorTesting.md[/font] - author mode, the debug functions and reading the why log
[*][font=Courier New]FollowerConversion.md[/font] - moving an existing faction-based follower to a profile file
[*][font=Courier New]SkyrimNet.md[/font] - the SkyrimNet bridge, word for word
[*][font=Courier New]OStim.md[/font] - what counts as a shared moment, for players and authors
[*][font=Courier New]Translating.md[/font] - translating the ledger through [font=Courier New]strings.js[/font]
[/list]

[color=#b8a285]An example profile ships in [font=Courier New]SKSE/Plugins/Romantasy/Profiles/ExampleFollower.toml.example[/font], inert until renamed.[/color]


[center][color=#382c1f]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#f59e0b]The Full Preference List[/color][/b][/size]

Every deed below maps to one vanilla statistic, in the same seven groups as the New bond page. The number is its point weight: each time the statistic goes up by one, a following companion gains that many points if she likes it or loses that many if she dislikes it. A favorite or pet peeve doubles the amount. Profiles accept the label or the [font=Courier New]ROM_*[/font] identifier.

